  "first_prompt": "<|im_start|>user\nA cake of 400 grams is divided into eight equal parts. Nathalie eats one-eighth of the cake, and Pierre eats double what Nathalie ate. How much did Pierre eat, in grams?\n\nThink step by step, then give the final answer on the last line as 'Answer: <number>'.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
  "first_trained_reply": "Here is the step-by-step solution:\n\n1.  **Calculate the weight of one part:**\n    The total weight of the cake is 400 grams, and it is divided into 8 equal parts.\n    Weight of one part = $400 \\text{ grams} / 8 = 50 \\text{ grams}$.\n\n2.  **Calculate how much Nathalie ate:**\n    Nathalie eats one-eighth of the cake, which corresponds to exactly one of these parts.\n    Amount Nathalie ate = $50 \\text{ grams}$.\n\n3.  **Calculate how much Pierre ate:**\n    Pierre eats double what Nathalie ate.\n    Amount Pierre ate = $2 \\times (\\text{Amount Nathalie ate})$\n    Amount Pierre ate = $2 \\times 50 \\text{ grams} = 100 \\text{ grams}$.\n\n**Alternative Method:**\nPierre eats double one-eighth, which is two-eighths ($2/8$) of the cake.\n$2/8$ of $400$ grams = $(1/4) \\times 400 = 100$ grams.\n\nAnswer: 100<|im_end|>\n"
